coder v0.0.0-devel

USAGE:
  coder identities

  Manage delegated identities (experimental)

  Aliases: identity

  A delegated identity is an identity for something that acts under you, for
  example a coding agent. It owns the workspaces created on its behalf, is named
  in audit logs, and can never do more than you.
    - Create an identity that may only read its own workspaces:
  
       $ coder identities create my-agent --scope workspace:read
  
    - Create a workspace on its behalf:
  
       $ coder create my-agent/task-1 --template docker
  
    - Change what it may do:
  
       $ coder identities update my-agent --scope workspace:read --scope
  template:read

SUBCOMMANDS:
    create    Create a delegated identity under you
    delete    Delete a delegated identity that owns no workspaces
    list      List the delegated identities below you
    show      Show a delegated identity
    update    Replace what a delegated identity may do

———
Run `coder --help` for a list of global options.
